"""Provider Normalizer — Phase 13G-3.

Transforms RawProviderSnapshot → Canonical Domain Model entities.

    RawProviderSnapshot
        ↓
    ProviderNormalizer
        ↓
    Canonical Domain Model (Physical, OS, Platform, Cluster, Node,
                            ExecutionEnvironment, Workload, Network,
                            Storage, Accelerator)

Architecture boundaries:
    ProviderNormalizer = deterministically transforms
    Verifier = validates
    Store = persists
    Orchestrator = coordinates

The normalizer does NOT:
    ❌ Connect to providers
    ❌ Verify data semantics (Verifier's job)
    ❌ Persist data (Store's job)
    ❌ Orchestrate workflows
    ❌ Infer/guess missing data
    ❌ Create INFERRED/UNKNOWN relationships
    ❌ Use LLM/heuristic/fuzzy matching

Relationship to existing BaseNormalizer:
    BaseNormalizer targets ServerInventory (inventory model).
    ProviderNormalizer targets canonical entities.
    They are NOT duplicates — different output models.

Reused from existing codebase:
    - All canonical entity classes and enums (models.canonical)
    - OrchestrationStatus, ErrorCategory (orchestrator.models)
    - RawProviderSnapshot, RawRelationshipEvidence (providers.base)
    - SourceEvidence, Confidence (models)
"""
